For every natural number n with 3 ≤ n and every real number κ with 4 ≤ κ, define the real numbers
r := (1 − 1/(n : ℝ)) ((√κ − 1)/(√κ + 1))
and
ℓ := (4(n : ℝ)√κ + (√κ − 1)²)/(8(n : ℝ)((n : ℝ) − 1)).
Then all of the following hold simultaneously:
(1) 0 < r;
(2) r < 1;
(3) 0 < ℓ;
(4) ℓ = ((κ − 1)/(8r))(1 + r²) − (κ + 1)/4;
(5) (κ − 1)/(2r) = (n : ℝ)(√κ + 1)²/(2((n : ℝ) − 1));
(6) for every real number u, both identities hold:
κ + 1 + 4ℓ − (κ − 1)u = ((κ − 1)/(2r))(1 + r² − 2ru),
and
((κ − 1)/(2r))(1 + r² − 2ru) = ((n : ℝ)(√κ + 1)²/(2((n : ℝ) − 1)))(1 + r² − 2ru).
Here √ denotes Real.sqrt, every occurrence of n in the definitions and identities is explicitly coerced to ℝ, and each subtraction involving such an occurrence, including (n : ℝ) − 1, is real subtraction.
